	file.0000000000000001.title: "Duckémon"
	quest.0036F53FBB26D934.quest_desc: ["This chapter covers some of the useful blocks and utility items that you can use while going through your Cobblemon adventure."]
	quest.0036F53FBB26D934.title: "Blocks and Utility"
	quest.031D1356DA5459EE.quest_desc: ["The Pasture Bin must be placed immediately adjacent to a Pasture Block with a Pokémon that has drops in order to collect drops. On a random tick (think wheat growth from vanilla Minecraft), the Pasture Bin picks a random Pokémon from a random immediately adjacent Pasture Block, tries to find a custom loot table from datapacks for this Pokémon’s species/form, rolls on that if it finds one, and rolls on the drop tables from the Pokémon’s Cobblemon species data if not"]
	quest.031D1356DA5459EE.quest_subtitle: "Passively Collect Drops from Pokemon"
	quest.03AC7927FE732BBE.quest_desc: [
		"A Trainer Spawner must be configured to specify the possible target trainers. This can be achieved by right clicking the block with any signature item that has been/can be configured for trainers. Supports multiple different items at the same time."
		""
		"This quests reward will let you pick the item needed to spawn the first trainer you need to battle to increase your level cap."
		""
		"&lHard Stone&r = Radical Red"
		"&lSmooth Rock&r = BDSP"
	]
	quest.042A1BBD38AB6477.quest_desc: [
		"The Display Case can be used to show off any item you think would be neat to display."
		""
		"Also used to turn unemployed villagers into Cobble Merchants to spend your Pokedollars."
	]
	quest.0EBBC5BE15A25A7C.quest_desc: [
		"Legends speak of trainers who discovered a way to push their Pokémon beyond their natural limits, awakening a hidden strength known as Mega Evolution. To channel this power, you will need a Mega Bracelet – a special trinket that bonds with your partner Pokémon’s Mega Stone."
		""
		"With the bracelet equipped, you’ll be able to unleash Mega Evolutions both inside and outside of battle, transforming your Pokémon into their most powerful forms. This isn’t just a cosmetic change – stats, abilities, and even appearances shift dramatically, opening up new strategies and challenges."
	]
	quest.11C4A30218D63EE3.quest_desc: [
		"When you assemble the Fossil Analyzer, you need to fill the Restoration Tank with organic material to bein analyzing fossils."
		""
		"Organic material can be any vanilla crop or raw meat."
		""
		"Once the restoration tank is filled, you can place a fossil inside of the Fossil Analyzer block to begin analyzing the fossil."
		""
		"After analyzing, use any kind of Pokeball on the Data Monitor to pull the restored Pokemon from the machine."
	]
	quest.1207D436772C5E19.quest_desc: [
		"A Pasture Block is a utility block that allows the player to deposit Pokémon from their PC into the surrounding area."
		""
		"The main purpose of the pasture block is to allow players to let out their Pokémon into a set area, being able to be interacted as if they were wild or thrown out of their ball. "
	]
	quest.130B71167D4D2CFD.quest_subtitle: "Used to fish up water Pokemon!"
	quest.1C10D64AC9BFC3C7.quest_desc: ["Some gyms don't have an exit block spawn inside of them, so it is important to bring something like the Exit Rope so that you can leave the gym at any time!"]
	quest.1D386CC6E1C39A08.quest_desc: [
		"The level cap is a restriction on how powerful your Pokémon can be. You can always check your current level cap by looking at your Trainer Card. This cap has two major effects:"
		""
		"&lNo More EXP&r: Any Pokémon in your party that is at or above your current level cap will stop gaining experience points from battles."
		""
		"&lBattle Refusal&r: NPC trainers will refuse to battle you if you have any Pokémon in your party that are even one level above your level cap. They'll let you know your team is too powerful for them right now."
		""
		"To increase your level cap, you must defeat the next key trainer in your series progression."
	]
	quest.1FC3D8E5CB24097F.quest_desc: [
		"/back = If you die, teleport back to the location you died. Only works on death"
		""
		"/tpa (name) = Send a tp request to someone to teleport to them"
		""
		"/sethome = Sets a home location for you to teleport to"
		""
		"/home = Teleports to the home location you set with /sethome"
		""
		"/cobbledollars = Allows you to pay other players and check the balance leaderboard "
	]
	quest.1FC3D8E5CB24097F.quest_subtitle: "Useful Commands"
	quest.1FD0C2B62EDFED8D.title: "Evolution Items"
	quest.22B6967798A8EB01.quest_desc: [
		"Open Parties and Claims adds the ability for claiming chunks and creating parties. Claimed chunks are protected from other players and can also be forceloaded so farms, machines, or Cobblemon spawns keep running while you’re offline."
		""
		"&lFTB Teams Integration:&r"
		"FTB Teams and Open Parties and Claims are separate systems. Land you claim is always owned by you personally, not by your FTB Team. However, FTB Teams has built-in support so that anyone in your team will automatically have permissions to interact with your claimed land. You can rename your claimed chunks to match your team name, but this must be done through the Open Parties and Claims menu."
		""
		"This means you can use FTB Teams for group progression while still keeping precise control over your land claims."
	]
	quest.2382E9CB58A48709.quest_desc: ["Radical Cobblemon Trainers introduces a structured progression system Cobblemon by adding a huge variety of NPC trainers to battle. Instead of just catching and exploring, you'll now follow a \"series,\" which is a questline similar to a traditional Pokémon game. You'll face off against rivals, gym leaders, and champions to prove you're the very best!"]
	quest.2398EADCCF75DADA.title: "Pidgey Possessor"
	quest.24537AB0F22CD0CA.quest_desc: [
		"The PokeNav shows all of the possible Pokemon that spawn in the biome you're located in."
		""
		"You can see all of the common, uncommon, rare, and ultra-rare spawns."
	]
	quest.2822040AB5E65427.quest_desc: [
		"Serene Seasons is a Minecraft mod that adds seasons. Grass and foliage colors will change throughout the year, and in the winter, temperatures will shift and allow for snow to fall in some biomes that don't normally receive any. Seasons also affect various other features, like crop growth, weather, and more!"
		""
		"There's also seasonal spawn/evolution conditions for Pokemon. Integrates Cobblemon's Seasons with Serene Seasons (think Deerling forms). Adds seasonal crop fertility for Cobblemon crops. Adds the following variants: Spring Espeon, Summer Glaceon, Fall Sylveon, and Winter Jolteon. These can be disabled/modified via datapack."
	]
	quest.29632F8B3F6B1723.quest_subtitle: "Like the PokeNav, but for fishing"
	quest.341E8D4D06F4F187.quest_desc: ["Everyday of the week has increased odds for shiny hunting! "]
	quest.39450F32B9753861.quest_desc: [
		"Open your PC from anywhere!"
		""
		"&lKeybind&r"
		"\\ = Open PC Storage (Requires equipped Box Link)"
	]
	quest.39D8F3AF45772C9C.quest_subtitle: "Scan all 1025 Pokemon"
	quest.39D8F3AF45772C9C.title: "Pokemon Researcher"
	quest.3CDC120997D195DA.quest_desc: [
		"Fully heals your party and removes all status effects!"
		""
		"If you craft and place one yourself, you must let the Healing Machine charge up before you can heal your Pokemon."
		""
		"Charging doesn't require any actual power and just takes time to charge. Each heal uses 10% of your charge at a time."
	]
	quest.3E962A75A750DEEE.quest_desc: [
		"Thank you for playing Duckémon!"
		""
		"This chapter covers some basic information about the modpack that could be useful for you while playing."
		""
		"Enjoy! <3"
	]
	quest.3E962A75A750DEEE.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to Duckémon"
	quest.420064C909E65445.quest_desc: [
		"The PokeFinder is used to find specific Pokemon species, aspects, or labels. You can even have it find only Shiny Pokemon."
		""
		"It can also pair up with the PokeNav to send Pokemon directly to the PokeFinder."
	]
	quest.42E3D92679B11E58.quest_desc: [
		"Below is a list of just some of the Cobblemon addons that are included with Duckémon. There are in total over 40 addons to Cobblemon that all add new things to the Cobblemon experience. (Note: You might need to scroll to read the list)"
		""
		"Cobblemon: Mega Showdown — Major gameplay expansion with Mega Evolution, Primals, Z-Moves, Dynamax, Ultra Burst, etc."
		""
		"Cobblemon Mass Outbreaks — Adds mass outbreak events (like in Legends: Arceus), creating exciting group spawns for hunting."
		""
		"Cobblemon Spawn Notifications — Alerts players when rare Pokémon spawn nearby, reducing missed opportunities."
		""
		"Cobblemon Ride On! — Enables riding Pokémon for travel — both functional and thematic."
		""
		"Cobblemon Recall Beams — Lets you customize the color/appearance of Poké Ball recall beams."
		""
		"Cobblemon Fight or Flight Reborn — Changes wild encounter behavior so Pokémon can engage in combat with mobs / adds extra encounter behavior mechanics."
		""
		"Cobblemon Alpha Project — Introduces Alpha variants (stronger/rarer spawns) — extra rare variants inspired by Legends: Arceus mechanics."
	]
	quest.43ED49C4D31FEBB5.quest_desc: [
		"Checking off this task allows you to immediately start the Brilliant Diamond/Shining Pearl series."
		""
		"&lIMPORTANT NOTE&r"
		"While you can accept both quest rewards to start both series, YOU CAN ONLY DO ONE SERIES AT A TIME. You will lose your progress if you switch mid way. ONLY ACCEPT ONE SERIES TO COMPLETE."
	]
	quest.5B5C88DF23BD6CFF.title: "Weedle Expert"
	quest.5E8170B681A205B9.quest_desc: [
		"Every Pokémon calls a specific environment its home. From the lush forests and frozen peaks to the blazing Nether and even the mystical Aether, each biome hides unique partners waiting to be found. Thanks to Terralith and Oh The Biomes We’ve Gone, the world is more diverse than ever, and Cobblemon fully embraces these landscapes."
		""
		"Exploring new biomes isn’t just sightseeing—it’s the key to expanding your Pokédex. Rare spawns dwell in caves, oceans, and even distant dimensions like the End. To become a true Pokémon Master, you’ll need to venture far and wide, seeking the perfect place where your next ally appears."
	]
	quest.68575FB43758CC36.quest_subtitle: "Pick your starter!"
	quest.68575FB43758CC36.title: "The World of Cobblemon"
	quest.68D7BED7A0EFD000.quest_desc: [
		"There a capture cap to prevent players from acquiring overly powerful Pokémon early in their journey. This capture cap is based directly on the level cap system from Radical Trainers."
		""
		"This means if your level cap is 15, you can only catch up to level 15 wild Pokemon."
		""
		"&lThis capture cap can be bypassed in two specific situations: &r"
		"- The cap is ignored if the wild Pokémon you are trying to catch is shiny."
		""
		"- The cap is also ignored when you use a Master Ball."
	]
	quest.6EC0EEA172FEC9C6.quest_desc: [
		"Checking off this task allows you to immediately start the Radical Red series."
		""
		"&lIMPORTANT NOTE&r"
		"While you can accept both quest rewards to start both series, YOU CAN ONLY DO ONE SERIES AT A TIME. You will lose your progress if you switch mid way. ONLY ACCEPT ONE SERIES TO COMPLETE."
	]
	quest.7172EC97B33E4F82.quest_desc: [
		"The PC is where Pokemon are sent when you have a full party or want to store Pokemon you don't want in your party."
		""
		"You can store 900 different Pokemon in your PC."
	]
	quest.7242A19A8BF26B45.title: "Fossil Analyzer"
	quest.73911B53492FF727.title: "Pokemon Grandmaster"
	quest.759014EB67E29F47.title: "Master of Karp"
	quest.76692C8D036682C4.quest_desc: [
		"Obtained as a rare drop when fishing with a vanilla fishing rod."
		""
		"Use the template, any fishing rod, and any kind of Pokeball to make a Poke Rod."
	]
	quest.77CB03DCC5F89E84.quest_desc: [
		"Place your Pokémon to roam in the pasture and come back later to maybe find an egg in the nesting area on the bottom of the pasture block."
		""
		"- Compatible pokemon breed if let in the pasture together, even with different owners."
		"- IVs inheritance, including function of Power items and Destiny Knot."
		"- Nature inheritance, including function of the Everstone."
		"- Form inheritance(1)."
		"- Ability inheritance(2)."
		"- Eggmoves inheritance. Every move the parents ever learned are included, so no need to equip them in their move set."
		"- Pokeball inheritance."
		"- Shiny hunting using methods similar to Masuda or Gen2 shiny breeding."
		"- Abilities reducing hatch time by half"
	]
	quest.787EA310C983CEB6.quest_desc: ["Stores berries for you to carry around. Also used for when fishing with a Poke Rod."]
	quest.79E3A2CCAFC527CE.title: "Competitive Items"
	quest.7B4708050C43E23E.quest_desc: [
		"M = Open Map"
		"B = Open Backpack"
		"C = Crawl"
		"Z = Zoom"
		"U = Emotes"
		"'  = Open Parties and Claims Menu"
	]
	quest.7B4708050C43E23E.quest_subtitle: "Important Keybinds"
	quest.7B6652E6F2B309F6.quest_desc: [
		"To keep track of your progress, you'll use a Trainer Card. This item shows you:"
		""
		"- What series you're on."
		""
		"- Your current level cap."
		""
		"- Which trainers you've defeated."
		""
		"- Hints on where to find the next key trainer you need to beat."
	]
	quest.7B6652E6F2B309F6.quest_subtitle: "Your Most Important Tool"
	reward.0A7ECB966D75FBD6.title: "Click me to begin the Radical Red series"
